cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please cite it as below, and please also cite the
  work it builds on: E. S. Egge and T. Mansour, "Bivariate generating functions
  for involutions restricted by 3412" (Adv. in Appl. Math. 36, 2006), where the
  weighted recurrence and Conjecture 3.14 appear, and E. S. Egge, "Restricted
  3412-avoiding involutions, continued fractions, and Chebyshev polynomials"
  (Adv. in Appl. Math. 33, 2004), where the ordinary conjecture appears. This is
  a proved theorem, machine-checked in Lean 4 from the definitions; priority
  is not established.
title: >-
  Reordering the indecomposable summands of a forbidden pattern does not change
  the bivariate generating function of 3412-avoiding involutions: a proof of the
  Egge–Mansour symmetry conjecture, formalized in Lean 4 from the definitions
type: software
authors:
  - name: "@AIOvernight"
    website: "https://x.com/AIOvernight"
date-released: "2026-10-19"
version: "2.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AIOvernight/egge-mansour-summand-symmetry"
url: "https://github.com/AIOvernight/egge-mansour-summand-symmetry"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - pattern avoidance
  - involutions
  - 3412-avoiding involutions
  - layered patterns
  - Wilf equivalence
  - generating functions
  - matrix Riccati equation
  - polynomial interpolation
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formal verification
abstract: >-
  For direct-sum indecomposable permutations tau_1, ..., tau_k, the bivariate
  generating function F(x,y) of involutions avoiding 3412 and
  tau_1 ⊕ ... ⊕ tau_k, with x marking length and y marking two-cycles, is
  invariant under every permutation of the summands, as an identity in
  Z[y][[x]]. For decreasing summands this is Conjecture 3.14 of Egge and
  Mansour (2006); at y = 1 it is Conjecture 6.9 of Egge (2004). The proof
  rewrites the Egge–Mansour weighted recurrence as a matrix Riccati identity
  AW - x^2 y W^2 = I with A bidiagonal, evaluates the full-interval series as
  p(1 - x) for an interpolation polynomial p through an unordered set of nodes,
  and specializes through a localization that inverts only 1 - x^2 y c_i c_j.
  The repository contains the manuscript, a Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of
  the whole theorem from the definitions of permutations, pattern containment,
  involutions and the bivariate series (including Guibert's decomposition, the
  containment lemmas and the Egge–Mansour weighted recurrence), and finite
  computational checks (exact enumeration to length 22 for selected layered
  patterns, exact symbolic identities for k <= 6). Theorem: proved and
  machine-checked in Lean 4 from the definitions. Priority is not established.
